9426	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s5","entry":{"id":"review-245e313fe1c041c281b44bc729916716","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:38:57.529Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The exclusions and per-job timeout policy reflect upstream user decisions.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md, 's5 decisions', explicitly accepts the listed exclusions, includes logout/switch/codespace cp/logs/ports, and retargets the HLD's 120-second limit to per-job limits. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain these decisions and file the acknowledged amendment.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every visibility change receives destructive approval.","evidence":"The design assigns codespace ports-visibility 'common 30', contradicting its destructive-visibility invariant. Installed gh help describes this command as 'Change the visibility of the forwarded port', including public visibility. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts]","action":"Classify ports-visibility as destructive and include it in approval tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Both existing display-cap tools already return data.truncated.","evidence":"ghPrDiffTool returns 'data: { number: n, diffBytes: body.length, truncated }'. ghRunViewTool instead returns 'data: { runId: id, jobs: payload.jobs ?? [] }'; truncation only affects its rendered heading/body. Its failed log command does currently use stderr as the log body. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts]","action":"Describe run-view data.truncated as an additive change, correct legacy fixtures and distinguish existing behavior from proposed behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current default and ten explicit gh timeout overrides match the design's inventory.","evidence":"helpers.ts uses 'opts.timeoutMs ?? 30_000'. The ten explicit calls specify issue create 60, pr diff 60/create 90/merge 180, run logs 60/workflow run 60, repo create/fork 120/clone 600, release create 180 seconds. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/issue.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/pr.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/actions.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/repo.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/release.ts]","action":"Use these values as the compatibility baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed no-input runShell path can supply stderrOverflow and aborted in the normalized outcome.","evidence":"ShellResult has neither field. runShell silently drops stderr beyond maxBytes; its abort handler only calls child.kill('SIGKILL'). runShellBytes separately reports both 'stderrOverflow: boolean' and 'aborted: boolean'. Thus the specified adapter cannot detect these conditions for ordinary gh calls. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Use runShellBytes for both paths or explicitly design the necessary shared-helper change with its ownership and callers addressed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Typed callTool and schema-checked text conversion already exist with the reusable shapes described.","evidence":"callTool<T extends TypedTool> derives input and output through Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. convertText(req, deps) validates schemas, invokes crossCheck with req.keyValues, serializes conversions and escalates once. [files: src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/convert-text.ts]","action":"Reuse these contracts without introducing parallel provider calls.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every new operation can accept repo and pass it as -R as specified by GhOpContracts.","evidence":"Installed gh 2.46.0 help for project create exposes --owner and --format, not -R; project field-delete exposes --id and --format, without --owner or -R. Config list exposes --host, without -R. The design nevertheless says 'all ops also take cwd and repo, passed as -R' and all project operations take owner. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/index.ts]","action":"Specify supported flags individually; omit or explicitly reject repo/owner for operations that do not support them. Define exact per-op schemas and argv rather than universal flags.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Preserving the historical snapshot and adding addedByS5 is sufficient for the planned approval and schema conversions.","evidence":"approval-class-mapping.test.ts still asserts 'assert.equal(tool.approval, common)' for historical requiresApproval-true tools except three git exceptions. It also deep-compares every historical input schema. Reading an addedByS5 list alone will not exempt the six historical gh tools becoming destructive or account for schema representation changes. [files: src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/fixtures/approval-snapshot.json]","action":"Specify S5 exceptions in the historical comparison loops, preserve baseline records, and test old-input compatibility separately from schema serialization identity.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes shared executor contracts and leaves workflow caller migration to s7.","evidence":"HLD §5.5 assigns gh schemas, classification and limits to s5; §5.7 assigns wrapper removal and caller migration to s7. Existing callTool and executor already provide typed invocation, schema validation and approval denial. The proposed tables and prose adequately identify these dependency directions; an ERD is unnecessary for these runtime contracts. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain this ownership boundary; resolve the shell-helper capability gap explicitly before implementation. No companion rendering was verified because none was supplied.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Any nonzero auth-status probe establishes missing-signin.","evidence":"Installed gh auth status help says it will 'test your authentication state for each GitHub host'. A failing probe is not proof of absent credentials: connectivity failures and failures for another configured host are not excluded. The design classifies any nonzero probe as missing-signin, overriding its separate unreachable/rejected semantics. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Scope probes to the command's host and retain probe diagnostics. Classify network/probe failures separately; require authentication-specific evidence for missing-signin.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The acceptance mapping covers all six actual upstream s5 acceptance criteria.","evidence":"DEF §6.5 defines coverage, checked results, destructive approval, missing installation/sign-in, timeout messaging and legacy compatibility as ac1–ac6. LLD §6 maps each to named coverage, integration, approval, failure, limit and compatibility tests. These are proposed tests, not verified passing implementations. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S005/LLD.md]","action":"Retain the mapping and add regression cases for unsupported per-op flags, ports visibility, historical snapshot exceptions, stderr overflow and failed auth probes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":5,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T10:38:57.529Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
